## GIT

To close it (stop watching):
Click into that PowerShell window and press Ctrl+C. That's it — stops instantly, nothing is lost, everything up to that point is already safely on GitHub. Closing the window with the X does the same thing.

To open it again (start watching):

Open File Explorer → go into the fo-sniper-fullstack folder
Hold Shift, right-click empty space → "Open PowerShell window here" (or "Open in Terminal")
Type "python auto_sync.py" and press Enter
Leave that window open while you work — that's the only requirement

That's the whole cycle: open a terminal there, run that one command, close with Ctrl+C when you're done for the day. No pip install needed again — that was one-time.



